# Repo layout

| Area | Path | Nx project |
|------|------|------------|
| Angular UI | `ui/` | `ui` |
| Nest API | `api/` | `@app-espn-lines-mono/api` |
| API features | `api/src/lib/<domain>/` | (inside api) |
| Shared packages | `packages/*` | (empty; future npm workspaces) |
| Local stack | `docker-compose.yml` | Mongo + API + UI |

API domains under `api/src/lib/`: auth, users, odds, events, picks, results, mailer.

# Commands (always via npm + nx)

```sh
# Full local stack (Mongo + API + UI)
npm run compose:up
# Wipe compose node_modules volume after major lockfile upgrades if needed:
npm run compose:fresh

npm run compose:down

# Host-only apps with Mongo in Docker
docker compose up mongodb
npm run serve:api
npm run serve:ui

npx nx show project ui --json
npx nx show project @app-espn-lines-mono/api --json
npx nx run-many -t lint,build
```

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill secrets before starting the API.

Angular 22 requires Node.js 22+ (CI and compose use `node:22`).

# Do not

- Invent Nx targets — resolve with `npx nx show project <name> --json`
- Assume an `apps/` / `libs/` layout (that is platform-nx-monorepo)
- Put shared packages at repo root — use `packages/*` when extracting shared code
- Assume a test runner is configured (Angular generators use `unitTestRunner: none`)

# Stack-specific rules

- Angular UI: `.cursor/rules/angular-ui.mdc`
- Nest API: `.cursor/rules/nestjs-api.mdc`
- Bootstrap + forms: `.cursor/rules/bootstrap-angular-forms.mdc`
